## 📊 Experimental Methodology & Results

1. **V-Dipole Audio Link:** Successfully demonstrated close-range audio reception with ~71 dB SNR; verified intelligible audio performance across extended distances and physical orientation shifts.
2. **Bidirectional QFH/V-Dipole Test:** Established a functional two-way link in both configurations, identifying baseline software buffering delays and local RF noise vectors.
3. **Offline NOAA Decoding Trial:** Executed a complete software dry-run using pre-recorded NOAA/Meteor audio files processed through SatDump/WXtoImg to validate the digital decoding chain prior to live capture.

---

## ⚠️ Current Challenges & Technical Roadmap

* **Noise Mitigation:** Investigating local RF interference, SDR gain optimization, cable losses, and impedance mismatches to improve signal margins.
* **Latency Optimization:** Analyzing software buffer sizes and sample rates across GNU Radio pipelines to eliminate audio processing delays.
* **Live Satellite Interception:** Moving from controlled local tests to full live-pass telemetry capture, incorporating real-time Doppler shift compensation and automated pass scheduling.
